% The REPL answers queries against the model the files defined and cannot
% change it (spec §59, §89), so the .stats it prints at the end still counts
% the program's two predicates and none of its own queries.  Blocks are not
% separated the way a batch run separates them: on a terminal the echo of
% what was typed does that, and here only the two queries sharing one line
% need a blank line between them.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
